From b7b6861b5a94b98fb65292c3607752f541f37a42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:15:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(budget): default monthly cap of 25 EUR for new
 companies, daily cap of 20% of it

A company with no org_budgets row used to have no cap at all. Now it gets
25 EUR/month; an owner can change it or clear it (a row with an empty limit
still means no limit). Companies that already exist keep their behaviour:
migration 0065 gives them an explicit empty-limit row. The daily cap is 20% of
the monthly one, so no schema change is needed. The cap applies to automatic
work, manual orchestrator requests and chat/MCP spending tools (spend guard).

Depends on fix/f1b (spend guard).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
